btrfs-snapman (0.7.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * New btrfs-snapman-cli: a curses interface and scriptable subcommands for
    terminals and SSH, using the same root helpers through sudo (or directly
    as root). Volume and location changes ask for the password every time.
  * Split into three packages: btrfs-snapman-common (helpers, config,
    shared modules), btrfs-snapman (GTK) and btrfs-snapman-cli, so headless
    machines install no GTK or polkit. libvirt-clients, needed only by
    the libvirt-fsfreeze hook, is now suggested rather than recommended.
  * Code shared by both front ends moves to snapman_client.py.
  * The journal names the caller via SUDO_UID as well as PKEXEC_UID.
  * install.sh --cli installs the terminal interface only.

 -- DarthDogCow <157978722+DarthDogCow@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:36:18 +0000

btrfs-snapman (0.6.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * New volume: "Browse…" next to Parent picks a folder. A folder that isn't
    a parent yet can be approved as a new location, with a snapshot root on
    the same btrfs filesystem.
  * New snapman-manage verbs add-parent and remove-parent, which write and
    remove /etc/btrfs-snapman/parents.d/<path>.toml.
  * load_config merges parents.d into the create parents, with the same
    ownership checks and skip-and-report handling as volumes.d.

 -- DarthDogCow <157978722+DarthDogCow@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:29:46 +0000

